---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Nintendo Entertainment System – Learn 6502 Assembly Through Games"
  description="Learn NES 6502 assembly by building complete games. Master the PPU, APU, and the processor that powered the console revolution."
>
  <style>
    .system-hero {
      min-height: 350px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e30613 0%, #ff4444 100%);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .system-hero::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(
          45deg,
          transparent,
          transparent 10px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 10px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 20px
        );
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .hero-content {
      text-align: center;
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .system-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      text-shadow: 3px 3px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .system-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .system-specs {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-top: var(--space-4);
    }

    .spec-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .spec-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      opacity: 0.8;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .spec-value {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      color: var(--color-text);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .section-intro {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
      max-width: 700px;
      text-align: center;
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    }

    /* Single Path Card */
    .path-container {
      max-width: 500px;
      margin: var(--space-8) auto 0;
    }

    .path-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #e30613;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .path-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(227, 6, 19, 0.2);
    }

    .path-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      color: #e30613;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .path-subtitle {
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .path-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .path-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      padding-top: var(--space-4);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .path-stat {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      color: #e30613;
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .path-cta {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
      background: #e30613;
      color: white;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-top: var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .console-note {
      text-align: center;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      margin-top: var(--space-8);
      padding: var(--space-4);
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .system-specs {
        gap: var(--space-4);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- System Hero -->
  <section class="system-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1 class="system-title">NINTENDO ENTERTAINMENT SYSTEM</h1>
      <p class="system-subtitle">Learn 6502 assembly by building games</p>
      <div class="system-specs">
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">CPU</div>
          <div class="spec-value">Ricoh 2A03</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Speed</div>
          <div class="spec-value">1.79 MHz</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">RAM</div>
          <div class="spec-value">2 KB</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Graphics</div>
          <div class="spec-value">PPU</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Sound</div>
          <div class="spec-value">APU</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Single Path -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Assembly Path</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The NES has no built-in programming language — everything is assembly. Master the PPU, APU, and the 6502 processor that powered the console revolution.
    </p>

    <div class="path-container">
      <a href="/nintendo-entertainment-system/assembly" class="path-card">
        <h3 class="path-title">6502 Assembly</h3>
        <p class="path-subtitle">Full hardware control</p>
        <p class="path-description">
          Learn the architecture behind Super Mario Bros, The Legend of Zelda, and Mega Man. Master the PPU for tiles and sprites, the APU for iconic 8-bit sound, and cartridge mappers for games that pushed beyond the hardware limits.
        </p>
        <div class="path-stats">
          <div class="path-stat">
            <div class="stat-value">18</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Games</div>
          </div>
          <div class="path-stat">
            <div class="stat-value">1,408</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Units</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="path-cta">Start Building Games</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="console-note">
      Unlike home computers of the era, the NES was a dedicated games console with no built-in BASIC. All NES development is in assembly — and that's what made it special.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
